CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17 --no-pointer-check --no-bounds-check
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*implicit arithmetic conversion not permitted.*$
^.*invalid explicit cast.*$
--
Verifies four operator-overload-resolution fixes:
  * ADL on a class declared at global scope walks the root namespace.
  * `operator_is_overloaded`'s 1st-option (member) path is skipped
    when T1 has no member operator.
  * `operators[]` includes `ID_mod` (`%`).
  * [over.match.oper]/3.4 restriction excludes free operators on
    unrelated class types when no operand has class type.
